---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import { weeklyPractice } from '../data/practice';
import { notesForWeek, noteHref } from '../data/roadmap';
---

<Base title="Practice">
  <div class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Drills for every week</p>
    <h1>Practice</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Reading a note takes an hour. Owning it takes problems. Every week here has hand problems, coding drills and a
      project milestone.
    </p>

    <Callout kind="plain">
      <p>
        Nobody learns to ride a bike by reading about balance. The notes explain each idea; the drills on this page
        are where you fall off and get back on. Interviewers can tell within two minutes whether you have done the
        problems or only read the answers.
      </p>
    </Callout>

    <h2>How to use this page</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <strong>By hand first.</strong> Paper and pen, no computer. These are the small calculations interviewers ask you
        to do on a whiteboard. Check your answers with code afterwards, never before.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Then code.</strong> Type every drill yourself in a fresh file. Before running, write down what you
        expect to see. When reality differs, that gap is the lesson.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Saturday is the milestone.</strong> Each week moves the current project forward. The milestone is
        done when it runs and has a test.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Keep a mistakes file.</strong> One line per mistake: what you got wrong and the rule that fixes it.
        Reread it every Sunday. It becomes your best revision document.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <Callout kind="note" label="Where the problem sets come from">
      <p>
        Khan Academy has graded exercise sets for every math topic in weeks 1–4; do the exercises, not only the videos.
        Deep-ML has LeetCode-style machine-learning coding problems that match our notes from week 4 onward. Kaggle
        supplies the datasets. Each week below links the exact pages.
      </p>
    </Callout>

    {
      weeklyPractice.map((w) => (
        <section class="phase" id={`week-${w.week}`}>
          <div class="phase-head">
            <span class="phase-number">W{w.week}</span>
            <h2>{w.theme}</h2>
          </div>
          <p class="schedule-track">
            <strong>Notes this week.</strong>{' '}
            {notesForWeek(w.week).map(({ track, note }, i, all) => (
              <>
                <em>{track.short}:</em>{' '}
                {note.ready ? <a href={noteHref(track, note)}>{note.title}</a> : <span class="pending">{note.title}</span>}{i < all.length - 1 ? ' · ' : '.'}
              </>
            ))}
          </p>
          <h3>By hand</h3>
          <ol>
            {w.byHand.map((p) => <li>{p}</li>)}
          </ol>
          <h3>Code</h3>
          <ol>
            {w.code.map((p) => <li>{p}</li>)}
          </ol>
          <h3>Saturday milestone</h3>
          <p>{w.milestone}</p>
          {w.resources && (
            <>
              <h3>Problem sets and sources</h3>
              <ul>
                {w.resources.map((r) => (
                  <li>
                    <a href={r.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                      {r.title}
                    </a>
                    {r.note && <> — {r.note}</>}
                  </li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            </>
          )}
        </section>
      ))
    }
  </div>
</Base>
